\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\i\f0\fs24\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Ring out, wild bells, to the wild sky,
\par The flying cloud, the frosty light:
\par The year is dying in the night;
\par Ring out, wild bells, and let him die. \i0 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Ring out the grief that saps 
\par the mind,
\par For those that here we see no more;
\par Ring out the feud of rich and poor,
\par Ring in redress to all mankind.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Ring out, wild bells, to the wild sky,
\par The flying cloud, the frosty light:
\par The year is dying in the night;
\par Ring out, wild bells, and let him die. \i0 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Ring out a slowly dying cause,
\par And ancient forms of party strife;
\par Ring in the nobler modes of life,
\par With sweeter manners, purer laws.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Ring out, wild bells, to the wild sky,
\par The flying cloud, the frosty light:
\par The year is dying in the night;
\par Ring out, wild bells, and let him die. \i0 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Ring out false pride in place and blood,
\par The civic slander and the spite;
\par Ring in the love of truth and right,
\par Ring in the common love of good.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Ring out, wild bells, to the wild sky,
\par The flying cloud, the frosty light:
\par The year is dying in the night;
\par Ring out, wild bells, and let him die. \i0 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Ring out old shapes of foul disease;
\par Ring out the narrowing lust of gold;
\par Ring out the thousand wars of old,
\par Ring in the thousand years of peace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Ring out, wild bells, to the wild sky,
\par The flying cloud, the frosty light:
\par The year is dying in the night;
\par Ring out, wild bells, and let him die. \i0 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Ring in the valiant man and free,
\par The larger heart, the kindlier hand;
\par Ring out the darkness of the land,
\par Ring in the Christ that is to be.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Ring out, wild bells, to the wild sky,
\par The flying cloud, the frosty light:
\par The year is dying in the night;
\par Ring out, wild bells, and let him die. 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i0\f1\fs16 
\par 
\par }

